closest-possible: generates the same deterministic assignment program, parses it, and checks the same AST count and final assignment name as Crystal. Crystal allocates a polymorphic object tree; this port stores tagged nodes in one bounded list and links children by integer index to fit next-lang's typed, pointer-free storage. The benchmark passes the vendored checksum but has a material AST layout difference, so it is reported outside the like-for-like headline.
